# G4's list for the cbp2025 host: the two traces the kit ships, symlinked
# into P2P_TRACE_DIR by cluster.yaml's worker setup.
#
# G4 asks one question: with the feature ON, does the host complete cleanly?
# It is not a score and it is not a direction check, so the right list is the
# cheapest pair that still exercises both integer and floating-point code.
# Each of these is about 1M instructions and finishes in a few seconds, so a
# broken port fails G4 in under a minute instead of after six.
#
# smoke-5.list is the older list and is five real training traces behind one
# sample trace. Six minutes of simulator per attempt is a slow way to learn
# that the binary segfaults.
int/sample_int_trace.gz
fp/sample_fp_trace.gz
